      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَبِيعَةٌ</span></b>  <i>A stone that is raised,</i> or <i>lifted,</i> (S, K,
TA,) <i>for trial of strength</i>: (K, TA:) applied
only to a stone. (Az, TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <i>A helmet of iron.</i>
(Lth, S, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  <i>A meadow;</i> or <i>a garden;</i> syn.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَوْضَةٌ</span>. (IAar, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A4-  <i>A</i> [<i>leathern water-bag, such
as is called</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَزَادَة</span>. (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>A kind of receptacle
for perfume and the like;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَتِيدَةٌ</span>, q. v. (K.)

